    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8275A\n\nSPONSOR: JACOBS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to authorizing the\nreclassification of controlled substances by regulation\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill will increase treatment options by allowing for certain drugs\nto be reclassified by the Commissioner of the Department of Health after\naction by the federal government.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: amends public health law by adding a new section 3307. This\nsection provides that, if a drug is rescheduled by the federal govern-\nment, the commissioner may reschedule the drug under New York State law\nthrough regulatory action\n\nSection 2: sets an effective date for this act.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Federal Drug Administration may reclassify drugs at any time\nthroughout the year. Should the New York Legislature be out of session\nat the time of these reclassification, drugs which otherwise would be\navailable to New York residents, will be unavailable until such time as\nthe New York legislature reconvenes and takes legislative action. This\nmay, at times, interrupt patients that are already using the drug under\nthe federal \"compassionate care\" program, which would end at the time\nthe federal government makes a drug commercially available. This legis-\nlation would serve as a measure that would allow the Commissioner of\nHealth to reschedule using regulatory action should he or she find that\nmay impair the health of patients.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
